  <h1 class="page-header__title">Paul Stamets and his work</h1>
  <p class="page-header__lead">
    An adapted overview of the biography and key research
    directions of American mycologist Paul Stamets
    (b. 1955): mycoremediation, mycelium extracts for bees,
    entomopathogenic fungi, mycorrhiza.
  </p>
</header>

<section>
  <h2>About Stamets</h2>
  <p>
    Paul Stamets is an American mycologist, author of "Mycelium
    Running" and "Fantastic Fungi", co-founder of Fungi Perfecti
    and the Host Defense brand. A detailed biography is in
    <a href="{{ '/en/stati/stamets-bio/' | url }}">"Paul Stamets: a short biography of the mycologist"</a>.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Main directions</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Mycoremediation.</strong> Degradation of hydrocarbons and pesticides, binding of heavy metals. Overview —
      <a href="{{ '/en/temy/mikoremediatsiya/' | url }}">the "Mycoremediation" topic</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Mycelium extracts for bees.</strong> A series of papers on the effect of supplements on viral load in honeybees. Overview —
      <a href="{{ '/en/stati/pchely/' | url }}">the "Mushrooms and bees" article</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Entomopathogenic fungi.</strong> <em>Metarhizium</em>, <em>Beauveria</em> and other species as biological control. Overview —
      <a href="{{ '/en/stati/entomopatogennye/' | url }}">the "Entomopathogenic fungi" article</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Mushrooms and immunity.</strong> Beta-glucans, PSK/PSP, innate-immunity receptors —
      <a href="{{ '/en/temy/immunitet/' | url }}">the "Mushrooms and immunity" topic</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Mycorrhiza and mycoforestry.</strong> The role of fungal networks in forest ecosystems and the idea of forestry built on mycorrhizal connections. Overview —
      <a href="{{ '/en/stati/mikoriza/' | url }}">the "Mycorrhiza" article</a>.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Books</h2>
  <dl>
    <dt>"Mycelium Running" (2005)</dt>
    <dd>Stamets's main popular-science book. An adapted overview —
      <a href="{{ '/en/stati/mycelium-running/' | url }}">the "Mycelium Running" article</a>.</dd>

    <dt>"Fantastic Fungi" (2020)</dt>
    <dd>The companion book to the documentary film of the same name (co-authored with Louie Schwartzberg and Evelyn Draper).</dd>
  </dl>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Species connected to Stamets's research</h2>
  <p>
    Stamets's materials and the Host Defense company catalog most
    often mention wood-decay fungi rich in beta-glucans and other
    bioactive compounds. Species cards — in the
    <a href="{{ '/en/griby/' | url }}">mushroom catalog</a>:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="{{ '/en/griby/reishi/' | url }}">Reishi (Ganoderma lucidum)</a> — a wood-decay polypore, one of the key objects in the Host Defense line.</li>
    <li><a href="{{ '/en/griby/agarikon/' | url }}">Agarikon (Laricifomes officinalis)</a> — a wood-decay fungus to which Stamets dedicated separate chapters in "Mycelium Running".</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>How we work with sources</h2>
  <p>
    In the site's materials we adapt Stamets's original texts and
    accompany them with links to the originals. Where Stamets
    formulates a hypothesis or a personal position, we mark it.
    Controversial claims are checked against independent
    scientific publications — collected in the
    <a href="{{ '/en/istochniki/' | url }}">"Sources"</a> section.
  </p>
</section>

